---
import StaticPage from '../layouts/StaticPage.astro';
---

<StaticPage
  title="How to Use a Scientific Calculator Online — Complete Guide | OnSciCalc"
  description="Complete guide on how to use a scientific calculator online. Learn trig functions, logarithms, exponents, fractions, keyboard shortcuts, and more with OnSciCalc."
  canonical="https://onscicalc.com/guides"
>

  <article class="prose-custom">
    <h1 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-ink font-geist tracking-tight mb-2">How to Use a Scientific Calculator Online</h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-ink/50 font-geist mb-8">A complete beginner's guide to using OnSciCalc, the free online scientific calculator.</p>

    <div class="space-y-8 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink/70 font-geist">

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-ink mb-3">Getting Started</h2>
        <p>
          OnSciCalc is a free online scientific calculator that works entirely in your browser. No downloads, no sign-ups — just open the page and start calculating. Type expressions using your keyboard or click the on-screen buttons. Press <strong>Enter</strong> to evaluate and <strong>Escape</strong> to clear.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-ink mb-3">Operator Precedence</h2>
        <p>
          OnSciCalc evaluates math expressions in standard algebraic order. Understanding this order is essential for getting correct results:
        </p>
        <div class="bg-canvas-soft border border-hairline p-4 rounded-md font-geist-mono text-xs space-y-1 mt-3">
          <div>1. <strong>Parentheses</strong> <span class="text-ink/50">( ... )</span></div>
          <div>2. <strong>Exponents</strong> <span class="text-ink/50">x^y</span></div>
          <div>3. <strong>Functions</strong> <span class="text-ink/50">sin, cos, tan, log, ln</span></div>
          <div>4. <strong>Multiplication / Division</strong> <span class="text-ink/50">*, /</span></div>
          <div>5. <strong>Addition / Subtraction</strong> <span class="text-ink/50">+, -</span></div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-ink mb-3">Trigonometric Functions (sin, cos, tan)</h2>
        <p>
          OnSciCalc supports all standard trigonometric functions. Type <strong>sin(30)</strong>, <strong>cos(45)</strong>, or <strong>tan(60)</strong> to evaluate. Toggle between <strong>DEG</strong> (degrees) and <strong>RAD</strong> (radians) mode depending on your needs.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2">In DEG mode: sin(30) = 0.5, cos(60) = 0.5</p>
        <p class="mt-1">In RAD mode: sin(pi/2) = 1, cos(pi) = -1</p>
        <div class="bg-canvas-soft-2 border border-hairline rounded-md p-3 mt-3 text-xs">
          <span class="font-semibold text-ink">2nd Shift Functions:</span> Toggle the 2nd button for inverse trig functions: sin⁻¹, cos⁻¹, tan⁻¹. You can also type asin, acos, or atan directly.
        </div>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-ink mb-3">Exponents and Powers</h2>
        <p>
          Use the ^ operator for exponentiation. Type 2^3 to calculate 2 to the power of 3, which equals 8. The 2nd shift button also provides x³ (cube) and eˣ (exponential function).
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-ink mb-3">Logarithms (log and ln)</h2>
        <p>OnSciCalc supports both base-10 logarithms and natural logarithms:</p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1 mt-2">
          <li>log(100) = 2 (base-10 logarithm)</li>
          <li>ln(e) = 1 (natural logarithm, base e)</li>
          <li>ln(1) = 0</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-ink mb-3">Factorials and Other Operations</h2>
        <p>
          Calculate factorials using the n! button or by typing 4! which equals 24. The cube root function is available in the 2nd shift mode. Use the square root button for square roots.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-ink mb-3">Parentheses and Implicit Multiplication</h2>
        <p>
          Use parentheses to control calculation order. OnSciCalc also supports implicit multiplication — typing 3(4+2) evaluates as 3 * (4+2) = 18.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-ink mb-3">Keyboard Shortcuts</h2>
        <p>Speed up your workflow with keyboard shortcuts: digits (0-9), operators (+ - * /), exponent (^), Enter to evaluate, Backspace to delete, Escape to clear, and Shift+S/C/T for inverse trig functions.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-ink mb-3">AI-Powered Suggestions</h2>
        <p>
          OnSciCalc features AI-powered suggestions that help you build expressions correctly. As you type, the calculator provides intelligent suggestions for completing your mathematical expressions, reducing syntax errors.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-ink mb-3">Dark and Light Mode</h2>
        <p>
          Toggle between dark and light themes using the theme button in the header. Your preference is saved automatically and persists across visits.
        </p>
      </section>

    </div>
  </article>

</StaticPage>
